    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Yordan Alvarez** (78.99) and **Junior Caminero** (76.84) anchor our lineup, representing our highest-ceiling plays. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a steady matchup against Avila and elite underlying metrics, while **Junior Caminero** faces the day\u2019s most favorable SP_xERA matchup (5.47), providing an ideal environment to capitalize on his power profile. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.06) also earns a strong recommendation despite his \"Lineup Pending\" status; his projected leadoff spot and a significant +14% boost from dynamic platoon factors make him a high-efficiency engine for stolen bases, a category we are prioritizing heavily today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision was bypassing **Carson Benge** (56.68) in favor of our current UTIL option, **Kazuma Okamoto** (52.73). While **Carson Benge** received a +5% boost from wind conditions and sits in the leadoff spot, our optimizer favored the situational leverage of **Kazuma Okamoto** against the LHP Weathers. Similarly, **Lars Nootbaar** (50.31) narrowly missed the cut; his platoon advantage remains high, but he simply lacked the raw score to displace the balanced efficiency of our starters.\n\nWe must remain cautious with our high-end talent facing elite arms. **Trea Turner** (49.46) and **Kyle Schwarber** (49.00) both face Misiorowski, whose 2.79 xERA is formidable, leading to a notable -19% SP skill penalty for both. Furthermore, **Christian Yelich** (46.66) is at high risk today; his score is dragged down significantly by a -13% platoon penalty against the LHP Banks. Managers should monitor the official lineup for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to ensure he retains that critical leadoff position, as any move down the order would necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of his projected value.",
